.TH EUCLID-CLI-ENS-LIST-MESSAGES 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ens-list-messages \- list a topic's messages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ens list-messages
.BR \-\-topic | \-t
.I ERN
[\fB\-\-page\-size\fR|\fB\-s\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-index\fR|\fB\-i\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-sort\-column\fR|\fB\-c\fR \fICOLUMN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists a topic's messages without changing their status. This is a
read-only, non-destructive inspection of the topic's contents, and is
paginated.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-topic " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the topic to list messages from. Required.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-page\-size " " \fIN\fR
Maximum number of messages to return. Defaults to \fI10\fR.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-page\-index " " \fIN\fR
Zero-based page index to return. Defaults to \fI0\fR.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-sort\-column " " \fICOLUMN\fR
Column to sort results by. Defaults to \fIcreated\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The matching messages are printed as JSON (possibly an empty list).
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or no topic
with that ERN exists.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens list-messages \e
    --topic ern:ens:eu-central-1:000000000000:topic:order-events

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens list-messages \e
    --topic ern:ens:eu-central-1:000000000000:topic:order-events \e
    --page-size 25 --page-index 1 --sort-column created
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ens (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-publish-message (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-get-message-count (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-purge-topic (1)
